From f99a5d667f5ae33d20d333de715f0d46fe43d067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Shields <noisyoly@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:23:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Plans: steering the score's chords, sections and structure

A request's harmony object steers the first stage while it writes the score:
recently used chords lose logits for their share of recent chord changes (by
exact spelling or by root), holding one root past a limit costs more each
bar, a section may not open the way the one before it did, roots outside the
key can be favoured while few recent chords are outside it, the names after
'%' can be held to a given list of sections in order, and a hook (a tune's
header and bars) can be held: the plan opens with its header and every
section of its name holds its bars.

The steering only adds to or takes from logits before the distribution, one
tracker per song of a batch, in plan-only jobs and in a full generate's plan.
Nothing asked for leaves the planner as it was.  /props lists the features
this build adds to the protocol.
